177 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 98 0 R
/T (Healthcare organizations collect data from admissions, diagnoses, procedures, medication orders and discharge records. These records can be analysed to understand patterns in patient outcomes. One relevant outcome is readmission within 30 days of discharge. A model that identifies patterns associated with this outcome may support research into discharge planning and follow-up processes.)
/E (Healthcare organizations collect data from admissions, diagnoses, procedures, medication orders and discharge records. These records can be analysed to understand patterns in patient outcomes. One relevant outcome is readmission within 30 days of discharge. A model that identifies patterns associated with this outcome may support research into discharge planning and follow-up processes.)
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
178 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 98 0 R
/T (Machine learning provides methods for learning statistical patterns from historical examples. In this project, the task is treated as binary classification: encounters labelled as readmitted within 30 days form the positive class, while encounters labelled as not readmitted within 30 days form the negative class. The system is an academic prototype and does not provide medical advice.)
/E (Machine learning provides methods for learning statistical patterns from historical examples. In this project, the task is treated as binary classification: encounters labelled as readmitted within 30 days form the positive class, while encounters labelled as not readmitted within 30 days form the negative class. The system is an academic prototype and does not provide medical advice.)
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
179 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 98 0 R
