<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/P 99 0 R
/T (Hospitals maintain extensive encounter records, but manually reviewing large numbers of records to identify patterns associated with 30-day readmission can be difficult. This project investigates whether selected patient and encounter attributes can be used by supervised machine learning algorithms to classify encounters as likely to belong to the 30-day readmission category.)
/E (Hospitals maintain extensive encounter records, but manually reviewing large numbers of records to identify patterns associated with 30-day readmission can be difficult. This project investigates whether selected patient and encounter attributes can be used by supervised machine learning algorithms to classify encounters as likely to belong to the 30-day readmission category.)
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
186 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/P 99 0 R
/T (The project predicts a historical outcome category; it does not establish that any patient characteristic causes readmission, nor does it establish that using the model will reduce readmission rates.)
/E (The project predicts a historical outcome category; it does not establish that any patient characteristic causes readmission, nor does it establish that using the model will reduce readmission rates.)
/Pg 15 0 R
