368 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/P 107 0 R
/T (Logistic Regression was selected for the demonstration because it achieved the highest F1-score \(0.2934\) among the three evaluated models. Random Forest achieved the highest accuracy \(0.8933\), but its positive-class recall was only 0.0005. This indicates that it identified almost none of the actual positive cases at the selected decision threshold. Accuracy alone would therefore give a misleading impression of its usefulness for the minority class.  )
/E (Logistic Regression was selected for the demonstration because it achieved the highest F1-score \(0.2934\) among the three evaluated models. Random Forest achieved the highest accuracy \(0.8933\), but its positive-class recall was only 0.0005. This indicates that it identified almost none of the actual positive cases at the selected decision threshold. Accuracy alone would therefore give a misleading impression of its usefulness for the minority class.  )
/Pg 23 0 R
/K [2]
>>
