672 0 obj
<<
/Title (This project developed an end-to-end machine learning prototype for classifying hospital encounters according to 30-day readmission status. It used the Diabetes 130-US Hospitals dataset and included data exploration, cleaning, target construction, patient-based splitting, preprocessing, model training and evaluation. Logistic Regression achieved the highest F1-score among the three compared models and was selected for the demonstration application. A Streamlit interface was created to accept CSV input and display predictions.)
/Dest [25 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 472 0 R
/Next 673 0 R
>>
endobj
673 0 obj
<<
/Title (The project demonstrates the practical stages of building a machine learning classification application. The evaluation also shows that high accuracy does not necessarily indicate good detection of the less frequent positive class. The current model is an educational prototype and is not suitable for clinical use.)
/Dest [25 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 472 0 R
/Prev 672 0 R
>>
endobj
