976 0 obj
<<
/Title (Logistic Regression was selected for the demonstration because it achieved the highest F1-score \(0.2934\) among the three evaluated models. Random Forest achieved the highest accuracy \(0.8933\), but its positive-class recall was only 0.0005. This indicates that it identified almost none of the actual positive cases at the selected decision threshold. Accuracy alone would therefore give a misleading impression of its usefulness for the minority class.)
/Dest [23 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 896 0 R
>>
endobj
977 0 obj
<<
/Title (For Logistic Regression, the reported positive-class precision was 0.1544 and positive-class recall was 0.5328. Its F1-score was 0.2934. This indicates that the model identified approximately 53% of the actual positive cases, although a substantial proportion of its positive predictions were incorrect. The model demonstrates a useful classification workflow but still requires improvement and further validation.)
/Dest [23 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 897 0 R
>>
endobj
